Normally, crash inside a loop is not a good practice, which we may involve more action on the crash later on.

We could do it like :
```
isSuccess = true
for ... {
    ...
    if err == nil ... {
        break
    }

    isSuccess = false
}

if !isSuccess { // or just check the for-loop condition, such as `i == retryTimes`
    // fatal actions ...   
    ...
    
    logutil.BgLogger().Fatal...

    // It would be easier to add more logic here.
}

```
